    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What sport needs both great strength and close teamwork on the water? The answer is rowing! In September 2025, Shanghai welcomed the world’s best rowers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The 2025 World Rowing Championships were held in Qingpu from September 21 to 28. More than 900 "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "athletes",
            "ref": "v-athlete"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from 56 countries took part. Along the river, they not only competed but also enjoyed the beautiful views of the city of Shanghai."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many famous rowers came for the event. If you are a fan of rowing, you must know Oliver Zeidler. He was last year’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "world champion",
            "ref": "v-world-champion"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the men’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "single sculls",
            "zh": "男子单人双桨"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". From China, we had Chen Yunxia and Zhang Ling. They won gold at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics. Many local fans came to cheer for them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "For lots of visitors, it was their first time in China. Here, they learned not only about rowing, but also about Shanghai. “The water is so clear,” said one audience member. “I can see rowers from all over the world. It feels like rowing is truly becoming a "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "global"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " sport.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The athletes were excited, too. One rower shared: “The place is beautiful. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "facilities",
            "ref": "v-facility"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " are great. I can see how much "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "effort",
            "ref": "v-effort"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people put into welcoming us. Everything is wonderful!”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Rowing used to be a less popular sport, but now more people are getting to know it. Through events like this, rowing is reaching new fans everywhere."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
